{
  "_comment": [
    "Seed scenario for the Clover unit. Fork-owned data, not code.",
    "Entity documents use Clover's own camelCase field names -- what the store",
    "holds and the wire carries -- so a documented example pastes straight in;",
    "the top level is snake_case like every other JSON this project publishes.",
    "Ids are 13 uppercase alphanumerics, the shape every Clover example uses.",
    "  order type id      https://docs.clover.com/dev/docs/creating-custom-orders (KFRPRVCZ73JHM)",
    "  Craft Beer at 750  https://docs.clover.com/dev/reference/inventorycreateitem",
    "  percentageDecimal  https://docs.clover.com/dev/reference/merchantgetdefaultservicecharge (percent x 10000)",
    "  tax rate scale     JUDGMENT, percent x 100000 -- see model/order.py TAX_RATE_SCALE",
    "The open order's total is client-set (750, its one line): Clover leaves",
    "totals to the app, and so does this fake. Timestamps are fixed (ms) so",
    "list filters are reproducible; token expirations are stamped at hydrate.",
    "The webhook subscriber is pre-verified (no `verified` key); its signature_key is the X-Clover-Auth code."
  ],
